# Normalize all text files to LF in the repo and on checkout (incl. Windows
# core.autocrlf=true), so committed goldens stay byte-identical to LF renders.
# This is a global default so a *new* committed golden/drift file with an
# unpinned extension is covered automatically — closing the recurring gap where
# .wit (#553) and .gitignore (#553) each had to be pinned individually after a
# Windows Tier-2 drift test caught the CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary markers so git never line-ending-munges these. None are
# committed today, but pinning the extensions keeps a future binary blob from
# being treated as text by the `* text=auto` default above.
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary

# Golden-file drift intent (retained from #553): these committed files are
# byte-compared against a fresh LF render on the Windows Tier-2 job and MUST
# stay LF. They are now covered by `* text=auto eol=lf` above, but the pointer
# is kept so the coupling to the tests stays discoverable:
#   - crates/tau-wasm-guest/wit-baseline/runner.wit vs generate_world(&[])
#     (tau-wasm-guest tests/wit_world.rs::baseline_equals_empty_generate_world)
#   - sdk/embed-js/.gitignore vs render_embed_js()
#     (tau-sdk-codegen tests/embed_js_drift.rs::committed_embed_js_matches_fresh_render)
